SUMMARY:City Architecture: The Annex\, Casa Loma and Spadina House!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass
  is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, emai
 l**\n[torontohistorywalks@gmail.com](http://torontohistorywalks@gmail.com%
 2A%2A/)\n**for more information or for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Ple
 ase note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for 
 this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n[torontohistor
 ywalks@gmail.com](http://torontohistorywalks@gmail.com%2A%2A/)\n\nGeorgian
 \, Gothic Revival\, Bay and Gable\, the list goes on and on. Toronto has m
 any styles\, and one can explore the history of Toronto simply by learning
  the different time periods involved.\n\nThis tour explores the **architec
 ture** of the Annex District\, **Casa Loma** and its grand competitor Spad
 ina House. These legendary landmarks on the hill overlooking the city have
  been focal points of Toronto history for well over a century in an area t
 hat has a vast story to tell.\n\nJust a reminder that we will be walking u
 p to the Case Loma site and exploring the grounds and the history\, we are
  not going inside any of the buildings.\n\nWe begin this walk in front of 
 the main doors to the Toronto Public Library Spadina Branch at 10 Spadina 
 Road. We end at St. Clair Avenue West at the Loblaws Superstore at the St.
  Clair West Subway Station. Hope to see you soon.\n\nThis walk is for most
  walking levels\; however\, there are steps and stairs near Casa Loma\, no
 rth of Davenport. Please dress for the weather and see you there.\n\nThe p
 rice of this tour is $15.00 per person!\n\n**Please note: Please e-transfe
 r the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-trans
 fer to the following email at:**\n[torontohistorywalks@gmail.com](http://t
 orontohistorywalks@gmail.com%2A%2A/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316693
 015/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260924T122454Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T122454Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_317325914@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061837Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T160000
SUMMARY:Historic Mount Pleasant Cemetery
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nThe only autho
 rized cemeteries within York were Anglican or Roman Catholic. Citizens who
  did not belong to either church had no choice but to find burial arrangem
 ents outside York.\n\nThe General Burying Ground received Royal Assent in 
 1826 and land that came to be known as Potters Field was acquired and star
 ted operation soon afterwards. Over time\, additional cemetery lands were 
 added and in 1873\, a new cemetery available to all citizens was establish
 ed. The new cemetery was situated on the farm land of the Cawthra family n
 ear Yonge Street.\n\nThis walk is for all fitness levels. Please dress for
  the weather. This walk will begin and end outside the Yorkminster Park Ba
 ptist Church at 1585 Yonge Street just north of Heath Street.\n\nThis tour
  has a ticket price of $15.00 per person! This tour has space for **11** e
 xplorers\, so if you do plan on attending please secure your tickets early
 .\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when bookin
 g your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:*
 *\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/317325
 914/
