BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_316974125@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061837Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T210000
SUMMARY:Christmas Lights of Toronto: Yorkville! (RETURN FOR 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nWe are back fo
 r another year of lights. Let's keep it going and celebrate Toronto!\n\nLe
 t's recapture the feeling of the holidays\, and celebrate the end of anoth
 er year. As 2026 begins to wind down\, a new year beckons. Let's enjoy the
  fall and take in the colour of the seasons. This tour explores the histor
 y of Yorkville at Christmas\, so it's a double tour of lights and history.
  Get your spots for this tour as soon as you can to be fully registered!\n
 \nResidents go above and beyond when decorating their homes and property. 
 The lights are exceptional and deserve to be shown off\, so let's look at 
 some of the most popular neighbourhoods when it comes to Christmas lights.
 \n\nAnd create a little Christmas magic in the meantime. Yorkville becomes
  a winter wonderland of multi-coloured lights. Let's explore this special 
 season.\n\nThe tour begins outside the Toronto Public Library - **Yorkvill
 e Branch** just west of Yonge Street on Yorkville Avenue!\n\n\\*\\* **Plea
 se note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for t
 his tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistor
 ywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316974
 125/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261014T124543Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T124543Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_316692905@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061837Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T140000
SUMMARY:Christmas in Old York! 1833 (RETURN FOR 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\n**If you plan 
 on attending\, please get your tickets for this event early as this tour h
 as run for the last 3 years\, and does sell out rather quickly.**\n\nSo wh
 at was it like in York in 1833 at Christmas time?\n\nThe prices of various
  food items and gifts on display\, the gas lights creating a glow as the s
 now begins\, places to gather\, places to get a drink\, like the Steamboat
  Hotel on Front Street\, or maybe one might decide to take their best girl
  or guy on a stagecoach trip to High Park to watch kids speed down the hil
 ls on their skids.\n\nWhat were the traditions in old York? Maybe the resi
 dents went down to the lake and watched the nighttime fishermen spear fish
  for Christmas dinner. Let's take a trip around old York and see what it w
 as like back in 1833\, three months before we changed our name to Toronto 
 in 1834.\n\nOr take a holiday trip to Kingston or Montreal to buy gifts di
 rectly from New York or London stores\, fancy hats for the ladies and ciga
 rs for the men. Books and wooden toys for the kids. What about that goose 
 in the little grocery store on King Street West of Jarvis? Candies from Br
 itain\, real home made gingerbread in the store windows.\n\nOn Christmas E
 ve everyone walked to St. James Cathedral for the ringing of the bells\, s
 inging\, and skating over the frozen Toronto Bay to the Peninsula.\n\nThis
  tour explores old York. This walking tour is for all walking levels. The 
 tour begins and ends at St. James Cathedral on King Street East at Church 
 Street. A great way to kick off the season.\n\nThis tour has a ticketed pr
 ice of $15.00.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amoun
 t when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the followi
 ng email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316692
 905/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260924T122115Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T122115Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_317023564@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061837Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T170000
SUMMARY:Lost Libraries of the Ancient World (LECTURES - 5TH ANNIVERSARY 2N
 D DATE)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pa
 ss is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, em
 ail**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for si
 gning up!**\n\n**A second date has been added as there are 9 on the waitli
 st for the Saturday October 24 lecture! If you are planning to take in thi
 s lecture\, get your spots early. See you then!**\n\nWe have an amazing "L
 ecture on the Go" series for 2026/2027. New topics and fascinating stories
  abound! Join me\, and uncover the world and keep active\, warm and cool d
 uring the winter and summer months!\n\nI started this walking classroom wh
 en we were under that horrible cloud called Covid. This series was popular
  and helped people get back into society and life. The first Lecture on th
 e Go was **Walking North America** and that was in October of 2021. Hard t
 o believe it's been 5 years of lectures. So I wanted to do something speci
 al to celebrate 5 years of exploration.\n\nThe "Lecture on the Go" Series 
 is open to members who have purchased the YEARLY MEMBERSHIP PASS\, it's fr
 ee for those members. If you wish to attend a lecture and you are not a ye
 arly pass member then the price **per** lecture is $20.00.\n\nLet's get st
 arted.\n\nWhat if some of humanity's greatest discoveries were made thousa
 nds of years ago\, and then lost forever?\n\nWhat if entire histories\, sc
 ientific breakthroughs\, literary masterpieces\, and eyewitness accounts o
 f the ancient world once existed\, only to disappear into the flames of wa
 r\, and the collapse of civilizations?\n\nJoin me for a fascinating journe
 y into the world's lost libraries\, from the legendary Library of Alexandr
 ia to the vanished collections of ancient empires whose treasures may be l
 ost forever.\n\nAt the heart\, stands the Library of Alexandria\, the most
  famous library in history. Founded over two thousand years ago\, it sough
 t to gather all the knowledge of the known world. Scholars from across the
  Mediterranean came to study astronomy\, mathematics\, geography\, medicin
 e\, philosophy\, and literature. Yet one of history's greatest mysteries r
 emains: what happened to this remarkable institution\, and what priceless 
 knowledge disappeared with it?\n\nWas it destroyed in a single catastrophe
 \, or did it slowly fade away over centuries from neglect?\n\nBeyond Alexa
 ndria\, we will explore a forgotten world of lost libraries and vanished c
 ollections stretching from Mesopotamia and ancient Egypt to medieval Europ
 e\, Baghdad\, and China. Discover the remarkable stories of librarians\, s
 cholars\, explorers\, and rulers who dedicated their lives to preserving k
 nowledge.\n\nWe will encounter lost books\, missing histories\, ancient sc
 ientific works\, and literary treasures that survive today only as fragmen
 ts.\nThis lecture is an exploration of one of history's most compelling qu
 estions: What have we forgotten?\n\nAnd how libraries shaped civilization 
 and why their loss continues to fascinate us centuries later. Whether you 
 are a lover of history\, literature\, archaeology\, or simply enjoy a good
  mystery\, this special Lecture on the Go will leave you wondering. What s
 ecrets of the past may still lie hidden\, just waiting to be rediscovered?
  Fascinating indeed!\n\nUpcoming topics in the 2026 series:\n\n\\*Philosop
 hy 1: Great Minds of the Western World: Goethe to Kant! - (2027)\n\\*Philo
 sophy 2: Great Minds of the Eastern\nWorld: Chuang Tzu to Dalai Lama - (20
 27)\nLegacy of Triangle: How a New York Factory Scandal changed North Amer
 ica - (September 2027)\n\nSo book your plans now!\n\nThis event is for all
  levels and walkers\, there are a few steps here and there to navigate\, b
 ut mostly on one level. This event in a non-walking event.\n\nThe lecture 
 begins on the steps of Old City Hall at the northeast corner of Bay Street
  and Queen Street West\, and\nhas a ticket price of $20.00 per person\, bu
 t **free with the yearly membership pass**.\n\n**Please note: Please e-tra
 nsfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-t
 ransfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/317023
 564/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261017T124036Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261017T124036Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_317361201@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061837Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T111000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T141000
SUMMARY:Christmas on the Historic Toronto Islands! 
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the f
 ollowing email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nIt's hard to im
 agine a better place than the Toronto Islands\, as the big day approaches.
  Christmas on the islands was full of tradition\, of skating on the frozen
  Toronto Bay\, and sleigh rides between Ward's and Centre. And if it snows
  well so much the better. Let's take a look back at the Christmas season o
 n the Islands.\n\nIt's about growing up in Toronto. About the ten minute r
 ide over on the ferry boat\, and the memories that have made Toronto a sum
 mertime and wintertime city. It's a stretch of land that is historic and f
 ascinating\, both geologically and socially as well. And a history that br
 ings together the stories of Toronto from its founding.\n\nThe Gibraltar P
 oint Lighthouse was constructed in 1809\, and is one of the oldest structu
 res in Toronto.\n\nThe peninsula was partially severed by a storm in 1852\
 , which created a sandbar that was dangerously thin\, and the peninsula be
 came an island permanently by a violent storm that cut out the eastern cha
 nnel\, two hotels on the island were also destroyed. The modern history of
  the Islands' begins here!\n\nThe Islands' have three main parts\, and all
  three have their historic elements\, the most being the western most isla
 nd named for the Hanlan family. A spectacular hotel\, "The Ned Hanlan" was
  built and a regatta course dredged out of the western lagoon. An amusemen
 t park followed\, and an airport after that!\n\nIt was also a residential 
 enclave with most of the homes appearing on Ward's and Centre Islands. And
  the Christmas traditions began. A winter wonderland of lights and laughin
 g children and some adults as well. Shall we explore the islands?\n\nThe t
